ConceptIntel migrations (Alembic)
=================================
Run everything from backend/ with the venv active.

Change the schema (add a column/table/index):
  1. Edit app/database/models.py
  2. alembic revision --autogenerate -m "add foo column to bar"
  3. READ the new file in alembic/versions/ (autogenerate is a draft, not magic)
  4. alembic upgrade head          # applies it, records it in the alembic_version table

Useful commands:
  alembic current                  # which revision the DB is on
  alembic history                  # list of all migrations, newest first
  alembic check                    # fails if models.py and the DB have drifted
  alembic upgrade head --sql       # print the SQL without running it
  alembic downgrade -1             # undo the last migration

One-time, on the existing database (already matches the models):
  alembic stamp head               # marks it as "at baseline" without changing any table

Legacy: scripts/add_*.py were the pre-Alembic manual migrations. They stay for history
and are all already applied. Do not write new ones - use `alembic revision`.
HNSW vector index: created by scripts/reembed_content_chunks.py, ignored by autogenerate
(see include_object in env.py).
